  "body": "In the [iso-2022-jp decoder](https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/#iso-2022-jp-decoder), in the \"trail byte\" case, when byte is \"end of stream\", the spec says to prepend the byte (which is end-of-stream) to the stream.  Am I misunderstanding ? If not why are we doing that ?",
